            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Applicable Scenarios and How to Use This Guide</h2>
<p>This SOP is designed for operations staff managing overseas advertising campaigns on platforms such as Facebook (Meta), Google Ads, and TikTok Ads. Compliance inspection is the first line of defense against account bans, rejected creatives, and budget waste. We recommend integrating these checks into your daily workflow, and new team members should complete their first full inspection within 3 days of onboarding.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Part 1: Daily Inspection Checklist (Approximately 15 Minutes)</h2>
<h3>1. Account Status Check</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Check Item</th>
<th>Normal Status</th>
<th>Action for Anomalies</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Account Balance</td>
<td>Shows current balance</td>
<td>If 0 or near warning threshold, verify recharge status</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Payment Method</td>
<td>Linked card/Pixel active</td>
<td>Switch to backup payment method</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Account Permissions</td>
<td>All staff can log in normally</td>
<td>Review permission list, remove departed employees promptly</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Violation Notifications</td>
<td>No new warnings</td>
<td>Enable push notifications to avoid missing alerts</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>2. Active Ad Status</h3>
<p>Open the Ads Manager and filter by "Status" column. Confirm the following:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>No "Ad Disapproved" entries</strong>: Creatives or copy triggered platform policies and need immediate editing.</li>
<li><strong>No "Pending Review" exceeding 24 hours</strong>: Extended pending status often indicates sensitive product categories or queue backlog. Consider streamlining creatives and resubmitting.</li>
<li><strong>Normal budget consumption</strong>: If an ad shows "Active" but zero spend, the audience may be too narrow or the bid is below the threshold needed for delivery.</li>
</ul>
<h3>3. Creative Review Status (Priority Focus)</h3>
<p>Log into Meta Business Suite or the respective platform backend. Navigate to "Ad Creatives" and review all review statuses. Key points:</p>
<ul>
<li>Creatives marked "Rejected" with reasons such as "Misleading Content" or "Sensitive Categories";</li>
<li>Creatives rejected 2+ consecutive times should be paused immediately to avoid triggering more aggressive account review.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Part 2: Weekly Inspection Checklist (Approximately 40 Minutes)</h2>
<h3>1. Historical Violation Review</h3>
<p>We recommend setting aside 30 minutes every Friday afternoon to review this week's violations.</p>
<p>Open the platform backend's "Account Quality" or "Policy Violations" page and record the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>Number and types of new violations this week;</li>
<li>Corresponding ad groups/campaigns;</li>
<li>Common patterns in rejected creatives (e.g., price comparisons, absolute claims, close-up portraits).</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Review Template Example:</strong></p>
<pre><code>Violation Type: Facebook Ad Policy Section 4.7 (Controversial Content)
Affected Ads: Product Line A - Summer Promotion Series
Problem Creative: Version 3 banner, contains &quot;100% Money-Back Guarantee&quot;
Resolution: Replaced with &quot;Returns and exchanges accepted,&quot; resubmitted for review
Prevention: Future refund-related copy will use platform-compliant language
</code></pre>
<h3>2. Audience and Geo-Targeting Compliance</h3>
<p>Some product categories have special restrictions in certain regions:</p>
<ul>
<li>Certain health products require additional qualification reviews when targeting EU audiences;</li>
<li>Financial ads have age lower bounds in some Southeast Asian countries;</li>
<li>Alcohol ads are prohibited from showing to audiences below specific ages in Japan and South Korea.</li>
</ul>
<p>We recommend checking campaign-level geographic and audience settings weekly to ensure alignment with product compliance requirements.</p>
<h3>3. Pixel/SDK Data Quality</h3>
<p>Open Facebook Events Manager or Google Analytics and check the following metrics:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Signal Quality Score</strong>: Below 5 indicates pixel installation issues;</li>
<li><strong>Conversion Event Volume</strong>: A week-over-week drop exceeding 30% may signal page technical issues or broken user paths;</li>
<li><strong>Duplicate Events</strong>: Multiple identical events from the same user may trigger platform risk controls.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Part 3: Monthly Inspection Checklist (Approximately 1.5 Hours)</h2>
<h3>1. Account Permissions and Team Audit</h3>
<p>At the beginning of each month, verify:</p>
<ul>
<li>Remove permissions for departed employees or third-party agencies;</li>
<li>Confirm all active staff have permission levels meeting the "least privilege" principle;</li>
<li>Check for unknown "Business Partners" or linked "Ad Accounts." If suspicious links are found, report immediately.</li>
</ul>
<h3>2. Policy Update Tracking</h3>
<p>Major platforms update advertising policies monthly. Operations teams should subscribe to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Meta Advertising Policies Updates page (monthly email notifications);</li>
<li>Google Ads Policy Blog;</li>
<li>TikTok for Business Creative Center Announcements.</li>
</ul>
<p>We recommend compiling a monthly "Policy Changes Summary" to share with team members, preventing compliance degradation of historical creatives due to policy updates.</p>
<h3>3. Account Health Scores</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Platform</th>
<th>Access Point</th>
<th>Health Standard</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Meta</td>
<td>Account Quality → Account Performance Rating</td>
<td>Score ≥ 6</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Google</td>
<td>Policy Center → Compliance Score</td>
<td>No serious violation records</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>TikTok</td>
<td>Assets → Content Safety Score</td>
<td>Green indicator</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>If scores continue to decline, consider pausing campaigns for the related product line and prioritizing root cause investigation.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Part 4: Quick Reference for Common Violation Types</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Violation Type</th>
<th>Typical Scenario</th>
<th>Emergency Response Steps</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Creative Rejection</td>
<td>First 3 seconds show comparison imagery</td>
<td>Delete controversial frames, re-edit and resubmit</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Landing Page Non-Compliance</td>
<td>Page lacks contact info or return policy</td>
<td>Add required information, request re-review</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Audience Misconfiguration</td>
<td>Health product shown to under-18</td>
<td>Pause campaign immediately, adjust age floor</td>
</tr>
